seg-b0c1eaeb4185 = <b>Source of the SEC-SIG layout.</b> The u-blox F9 HPG { "1.32" } and M10 SPG { "5.10" } interface descriptions that could be downloaded when this was written name UBX-SEC-SIG but do not define it. The layouts above are those of the later u-blox interface descriptions as transcribed in the pyubx2 library (BSD-3-Clause, <c1/> and <c2/>); the fixture tests in <c3/> are built from that layout, not from a real receiver's output. Layout from open transcription, not checked against the current vendor guide: check it against the current u-blox interface description before relying on SEC-SIG.

# text
seg-6af7d45be34d = A SEC-SIG has no time of week; it belongs to the current navigation epoch. A state already read at an epoch is kept unless a later one is worse.

