seg-f30ddb83bf99 = Where a log carries these flags, every epoch of the result has <c1/> (the two states, whether the receiver flags, whether any Kshana monitor alarmed, and <c2/>: <c3/>, <c4/>, <c5/>, <c6/>, or <c7/>), and the result has <c8/> with the counts and the first epoch of each. The receiver "flags" at a state of { "2" } or more. It <b>raises no alarm and changes no score</b>, and neither side is ground truth: agreement is not validation, and a disagreement says one detector saw something the other did not, nothing about which was right. Studio's strip reads <c9/>.

