seg-4d6365d9ffd1 = <c1/> decodes with the <c2/> crate ({ "0.4" }, <b>MIT</b>; its only dependency is <c3/>; a permissive licence that <c4/> allows). Blocks read: PVTGeodetic ({ "4007" }) for the fix, MeasEpoch ({ "4027" }) for C/N0 per satellite and signal (<c5/> is the signal's name, such as <c6/>), and RFStatus ({ "4092" }) for the number of RF bands whose <c7/> byte is non-zero (<c8/>, carried and <b>not interpreted</b>: it never counts as a flag). Epochs are keyed by time of week and week number and labelled in GPS time (<c9/>). A block failing its CRC or parse counts as a skipped record. This reader does not read AGC or a jamming indicator, so the C/N0-drop and loss-of-lock monitors run and the AGC and jamming-indicator monitors do not.

